    {
      "id": 188749,
      "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
      "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
      "created_at": "2017-02-07T04:28:26.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>From the title, I was expecting Ra and fellows against Gloomy, Apostate, or the Matriarch. &nbsp;Imagine my surprise when I got none of those things. &nbsp;I supose the \"Museum\" should have been a clue. &nbsp;Oh well.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Mint. &nbsp;I was too careless with Parse's attacks on Miss Info, and she got knocked out soon after the flip. &nbsp;But she did a great job of manipulating the deck before that, and got in some good hits. &nbsp;So that was fine. &nbsp;I intentionally let the Wrathful Retribution slip away to kill that first diversion. &nbsp;Maybe not the best choice, but Fanatic did very well without it. &nbsp;KNYFE spent the first half the game bored and lonely, but she quickly made up for it on the other end.</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:14:46.874Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 16153,
      "topic_slug": "weekly-one-shot-60-it-belongs-in-a-museum",
